          "id": "b01",
          "text": "Let's solve this one step by step. How many factors are multiplied in the term six x squared y?",
          "display": "6x^2y",
          "cue": "show-problem",
          "pause_after_s": 1.2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "title": "Step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b02",
          "text": "Factors are the things multiplied inside a term. Start by writing the term as a product: six times x squared times y.",
          "display": "6 · x · x · y",
          "cue": "step-1"
        },
        {
          "id": "b03",
          "text": "Now x squared means x times x. So the factors are six, x, x and y. That is four.",
          "display": "4 factors",
          "cue": "step-2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "title": "The answer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b04",
          "text": "So the answer is four.",
          "display": "4",
          "cue": "answer"
        },
        {
          "id": "b05",
          "text": "Watch out for these traps. If you counted x squared as one factor, you get three. If you counted only the letters x and y, you get two.",
          "cue": "traps"
        }
      ]
    }
